    "_estimator": "Plug-in MI on discrete joint counts (NOT KSG -- KSG fails on binary inputs)",
    "_methodology_note": "V5e uses binary {0, 1} integer inputs. The apparatus's _kraskov_mi (sklearn mutual_info_regression with PCA + KSG nearest neighbors) structurally underestimates joint MI for synergistic relationships on binary data, because nearest-neighbor distances do not reflect XOR-style structure. Plug-in MI on the empirical joint distribution is exact for V5e's finitely-supported distribution. V5b stays KSG (continuous data, KSG works). The empirical fleet uses R_kNN (marginal-MI-share, a different quantity than II/I_total), so the plug-in/KSG split does not introduce a fleet-vs-calibration inconsistency.",
